 "closes": true,
 "closes_note": "ALL SIXTEEN FOOTED COLUMNS CLOSE EXACTLY - seven of seven in the male block, nine of nine in the female block. That is the check on the grid as much as on the reading: the same band-fitted column grid, read the same way, reproduces the enumerator's own arithmetic over 113 people. ONE MARK WAS REFUSED to get there and it is named rather than buried: a small horizontal flick stands inside the male 'under 5' cell of line 30 (Henry Bowen), 57 px of eroded ink where a tally stroke on this sheet carries 90 to 220. It is not a numeral form, it lies on the path of the sweeping tail this hand gives the name above it, and it is recorded as no entry. Had it been read as a 1 the male under-5 column would foot 4 against the enumerator's 3. The reading was not adjusted to the total - the mark was judged on the page, and its exclusion is stated here so a later reader can overturn it.",
